# CODEOWNERS — Fulcrum AI COE POC
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Route PR reviews to the right owner based on what changed.
# GitHub enforces these as required reviewers when branch protection is on.
#
# Format: <path pattern>  <@owner or team>
# Last matching rule wins for a given file.
#
# Teams to create in your GitHub org:
#   @<org>/coe-engineering   — DevSavant engineers
#   @<org>/coe-security      — Fulcrum security / compliance
#   @<org>/coe-operations    — Fulcrum operations / COE owners
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Default: everything needs engineering + security review
*  @<org>/coe-engineering @<org>/coe-security

# Workflow YAML changes always include security
.github/workflows/  @<org>/coe-engineering @<org>/coe-security

# Autofix commits — security must approve before merge
autofix-summary.md  @<org>/coe-security @<org>/coe-operations

# n8n workflow JSON — operations owner approves
workflows/          @<org>/coe-engineering @<org>/coe-operations

# Documentation and playbooks — COE operations + engineering
docs/               @<org>/coe-engineering @<org>/coe-operations

# Source — engineering lead owns
src/                @<org>/coe-engineering

# Infrastructure / deployment config — security + engineering
infra/              @<org>/coe-engineering @<org>/coe-security

# Dependency manifests — security always reviews
src/package.json    @<org>/coe-security @<org>/coe-engineering
src/package-lock.json  @<org>/coe-security
requirements.txt    @<org>/coe-security
go.mod              @<org>/coe-security
go.sum              @<org>/coe-security
